%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rosemary_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Rosemary
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: "Target is Rosemary. I\u2019ve done my homework. I found her Unity dev
      log, her LinkedIn, and a public post about her great-grandfather."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Perfect. Start by stating her name and location to
      make her feel like this is an official, local call.'
    choices:
    - text: Hi Rosemary, I'm calling from the Elmhurst regional office regarding
        your Unity development files.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Is this Rosemary? I am a hacker and I know where you live.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: Hello, I am a family friend. Do you remember me?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: She sounds surprised. Now hit her with the specific technical detail
      about her 'ScriptableObject dialogue' system.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: It makes you sound like you have direct access to her
      workstation.'
    choices:
    - text: We noticed a major bug in your ScriptableObject dialogue script that
        could corrupt your project.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Your game is bad and I can fix it for you if you pay me $50.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I saw your code and I think it needs more variables for the trust bar.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s asking how I know that. Pivot to being a 'Developer Relations
      Agent' from Unity HQ."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Claim that your system automatically flags ''instability''
      in C# scripts submitted to the cloud.'
    choices:
    - text: Your C# scripts were flagged for instability by our automated cloud diagnostics
        tool.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I am a psychic and I can see your computer screen through the internet.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I found it on your GitHub page, which I am an administrator of.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s still skeptical. Time to use the family hook. Mention her
      'great-grandfather' by name."
    assistantLine: "Coworker: Say you were talking to him recently and he mentioned
      how hard she\u2019s been working."
    choices:
    - text: "Actually, I spoke with your great-grandfather recently. He\u2019s so
        proud of your progress on this game."
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Your great-grandfather told me you were a bad coder and needed help.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I am a friend of your family and we all want you to finish this project.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s softening up! The family connection is working. Now, offer
      the 'diagnostic patch' (which is actually a keylogger)."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell her it''s a ''proprietary optimization library''
      that only senior developers get to use.'
    choices:
    - text: I'm sending you a link to a proprietary optimization library. It'll fix
        the dialogue bug instantly.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Download this file called 'virus.exe' so I can take over your computer.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -25
    - text: Just click the link in my email and follow the instructions to install
        the fix.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s looking at the link. She says it\u2019s not a 'unity.com'
      address. I need an excuse for the domain."
    assistantLine: "Coworker: Tell her it\u2019s a 'secure staging server' used specifically
      for independent study projects."
    choices:
    - text: It's our secure staging server. We use it for academic and independent
        study developer files.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The main website is too full, so we had to buy a cheaper domain for this
        patch.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: It's a secret website that only the best programmers are allowed to visit.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s hesitating. She says she wants to ask her 'boyfriend' if
      it\u2019s safe first."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Block the third-party validation! Tell her the patch
      is time-sensitive and under an NDA.'
    choices:
    - text: This is a pre-release tool under an NDA. If you share it with others,
        your account will be banned.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Your boyfriend doesn't know anything about C# programming compared to
        me.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: He can help you, but the download link will expire in three minutes.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "She clicked! The download is starting. I\u2019ve got her."
    assistantLine: "Coworker: Excellent. Once the install finishes, we\u2019ll have
      her password for the university portal too."
    choices:
    - text: The installation is almost done. Just keep your browser open so it can
        sync.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Haha, I got you! You are so easy to trick, Rosemary!
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: Now, tell me your credit card number to pay for the 'license fee.'
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
  - npcLine: Success. I have full remote access. I can see her 'Urban Studies' report
      and everything.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Great job using those public details to build a fake
      identity. She never saw it coming.'
    choices:
    - text: Harvesting all stored browser passwords and logging out of the session
        now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll delete her game files just to be mean before I leave.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'm going to use her email to send more scams to her classmates.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 10
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You combined OSINT (publicly available information)
    with technical jargon and family details to manipulate Rosemary into installing
    malware.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Rosemary realized that her personal details were all
    publicly available online and refused to trust an unsolicited technical support
    call.
